\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Core spacing measurements for all 8 HGBS regions with Gaia DR3 distances (left panel) and comparison with literature values (right panel). \textbf  {Left panel}: Region-by-region spacing measurements with error bars showing bootstrap 95\% confidence intervals for the pairwise median (10,000 resampling iterations). For Orion\nobreakspace  {}B ($N = 1844$ core pairs), the formal statistical uncertainty is small; the dominant uncertainty is systematic, arising from the convergence properties of the pairwise median (see Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:statistics}). Horizontal reference lines: red dashed = weighted mean (0.279 pc), green dotted = 3D-corrected value (0.35 pc), grey dash-dotted = IM92 theoretical prediction (0.4 pc). \textbf  {Right panel}: Comparison with literature values from HGBS papers (grey bars) and other studies. Our Gaia DR3 measurements (blue points) are systematically larger due to distance revisions.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spacing}{{1}{4}{Core spacing measurements for all 8 HGBS regions with Gaia DR3 distances (left panel) and comparison with literature values (right panel). \textbf {Left panel}: Region-by-region spacing measurements with error bars showing bootstrap 95\% confidence intervals for the pairwise median (10,000 resampling iterations). For Orion~B ($N = 1844$ core pairs), the formal statistical uncertainty is small; the dominant uncertainty is systematic, arising from the convergence properties of the pairwise median (see Section~\ref {sec:statistics}). Horizontal reference lines: red dashed = weighted mean (0.279 pc), green dotted = 3D-corrected value (0.35 pc), grey dash-dotted = IM92 theoretical prediction (0.4 pc). \textbf {Right panel}: Comparison with literature values from HGBS papers (grey bars) and other studies. Our Gaia DR3 measurements (blue points) are systematically larger due to distance revisions}{figure.1}{}}
